  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 152 AM CDT CDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nThe upper-level ridge will remain centered near the Four Corners \nlate this weekend through the middle of next week. This feature may \nweaken somewhat by the latter part of the week but should still \ncontinue to extend from the Four Corners through the state of Texas \nand the Gulf Coast region. Hot and dry weather conditions will \ncontinue for most of our forecast area Sunday through Tuesday with \nthe exception of very isolated convection near the Davis Mountains \nor Marfa Plateau. Shower and storm coverage may become more \nscattered in nature (generally 30-50%) by Wednesday and Thursday \nover the Guadalupe/Davis Mountains and down into the Marfa Plateau \nand Big Bend, while POPs over the rest of the forecast area remain \n20% or less. Expect the August heat to persist through much of next \nweek with daily highs ranging in the upper 90s to around 102 degrees \nfor most locations each day. A few places along the Rio Grande \nmay top out between 103-108 degrees next week.",
